{"slug":"triples-with-zero-and","title":"Count the Triples Whose AND Is Zero","topic":"greedy-bits","difficulty":"hard","order":895,"tags":["bit-manipulation","sos-dp","submasks","counting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Count the ANDs of all pairs first, then ask how many numbers fit inside the complement of each pair-AND","body":["Count the **ordered triples** of positions `(i, j, k)` (the positions may repeat) such that `a[i] & a[j] & a[k] == 0`. For the list `2 1 3` the answer is 12. Trying all `n^3` triples is 10^9 steps for `n = 1000`. The numbers are small (below `2^16 = 65536`), and this will be used.","Split the triple into a pair and a single number. Let `pairs[x]` be the number of ordered pairs `(i, j)` with `a[i] & a[j] = x`: there are `n^2 = 10^6` pairs, so this takes a million steps. For a given `x`, the number `a[k]` works if `x & a[k] == 0`, that is, if every bit of `a[k]` is **outside** `x`: `a[k]` is a **submask of the complement** `~x` (within 16 bits). So we need `f[m]`, the number of values `a[k]` that are submasks of `m`, for every mask `m`. The answer is the sum of `pairs[x] * f[~x]` over all `x`.",{"code":"FULL = (1 << 16) - 1\nf = [0] * (1 << 16)\nfor v in a: f[v] += 1\nfor b in range(16):                       # sum over submasks (SOS DP)\n    for m in range(1 << 16):\n        if (m >> b) & 1:\n            f[m] += f[m ^ (1 << b)]\npairs = [0] * (1 << 16)\nfor x in a:\n    for y in a: pairs[x & y] += 1\nanswer = sum(pairs[x] * f[FULL ^ x] for x in range(1 << 16))"},"The table `f` is built by the **sum-over-subsets** transform: process the bits one by one, and for every mask that has the bit add the value of the mask without the bit. After all 16 bits, `f[m]` holds the number of values that are submasks of `m`. The cost is `16 * 65536` steps. Together with the million pairs the program runs in about 2 * 10^6 steps instead of 10^9; the answer is at most `n^3 = 10^9`."]},"statement":["A list of `n` numbers (all below 65536) is given. Count the ordered triples of positions `(i, j, k)`, where the positions need not be different, for which `a[i] & a[j] & a[k] = 0`."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`: the number of values.","The second line has `n` numbers."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of triples."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","0 <= each number < 2^16"],"examples":[{"input":"3\n2 1 3\n","output":"12\n","note":"The triples (in any order of positions) with AND 0 number 12."}],"hints":["Count first how many ordered pairs have each possible AND value.","A number fits with the pair AND x when it is a submask of the complement of x.","Compute \"number of values that are submasks of m\" for all m with the sum-over-subsets transform."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["The numbers of ordered pairs with each AND value are counted; a sum-over-subsets transform gives, for every mask, how many numbers are its submasks; the answer sums pairs[x] times the count of numbers inside the complement of x."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2 + 16 * 2^16), space O(2^16).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nsize = 1 << 16\nfull = size - 1\nf = [0] * size\nfor v in a:\n    f[v] += 1\nfor b in range(16):\n    bit = 1 << b\n    for m in range(size):\n        if m & bit:\n            f[m] += f[m ^ bit]\npairs = [0] * size\nfor x in a:\n    for y in a:\n        pairs[x & y] += 1\ntotal = 0\nfor x in range(size):\n    if pairs[x]:\n        total += pairs[x] * f[full ^ x]\nprint(total)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    const int SIZE = 1 << 16, FULL = SIZE - 1;\n    vector<long long> f(SIZE, 0), pairs(SIZE, 0);\n    for (long long v : a) f[v]++;\n    for (int b = 0; b < 16; b++) {\n        for (int m = 0; m < SIZE; m++) {\n            if (m & (1 << b)) f[m] += f[m ^ (1 << b)];\n        }\n    }\n    for (long long x : a) {\n        for (long long y : a) pairs[x & y]++;\n    }\n    long long total = 0;\n    for (int x = 0; x < SIZE; x++) total += pairs[x] * f[FULL ^ x];\n    cout << total << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        int size = 1 << 16, full = size - 1;\n        long[] f = new long[size];\n        long[] pairs = new long[size];\n        for (long v : a) f[(int) v]++;\n        for (int b = 0; b < 16; b++) {\n            for (int m = 0; m < size; m++) {\n                if ((m & (1 << b)) != 0) f[m] += f[m ^ (1 << b)];\n            }\n        }\n        for (long x : a) {\n            for (long y : a) pairs[(int) (x & y)]++;\n        }\n        long total = 0;\n        for (int x = 0; x < size; x++) total += pairs[x] * f[full ^ x];\n        System.out.println(total);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3\n2 1 3\n","output":"12\n"},{"input":"1\n0\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"1\n1\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"2\n65535 65535\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"3\n1 2 4\n","output":"24\n"},{"input":"10\n71 60 61 16 2 32 42 80 40 8\n","output":"708\n"},{"input":"100\n7249 46687 33249 49489 28555 13767 57645 56829 47871 57810 48742 19161 2037 46735 11793 2586 40955 34250 47983 39729 7872 31395 41090 15509 19038 3656 20291 14124 26798 29790 5051 26790 48410 12091 11613 32383 55098 8752 58635 9210 37674 60181 15892 60742 18603 43269 10167 30213 22981 31694 5674 51766 44459 48161 28142 17606 7640 26219 41065 48971 39463 5132 34659 25618 61721 49339 4548 32512 10320 51360 65320 28129 12883 7971 60185 33711 8814 26732 2601 4577 6074 20119 58187 54508 56380 1263 21006 11248 29346 282 22009 48168 41421 3042 16281 65036 35065 8146 25536 34727\n","output":"113550\n"},{"input":"1000\n15793 34779 33014 11709 28515 26582 51901 33351 25686 22215 44387 25964 26157 28393 22306 35141 53235 46484 60579 40431 59766 14437 7854 52585 2040 916 8239 30994 17584 21998 37129 26823 51080 47841 62654 65384 43601 595 16892 36459 30017 42414 37826 56358 712 29578 51383 44881 40361 23376 2962 25937 51041 24894 52029 292 38786 47080 61618 44463 55790 12108 9739 4398 13382 61289 30627 45675 49638 41